        ":question/problem": "Calculate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ if $f(x)=2x+{e}^{4x-6}.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $y={e}^{4x-6}$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=4x-6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the sum rule of differentiation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+{e}^{4x-6}) \\\\  & =2+4{e}^{4x-6} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x-6}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
