        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-4{e}^{u}-3,\\,u=3x-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-4{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-12{e}^{3x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=2} & =-12{e}^{3x-5}{|}_{x=2} \\\\ & =-12{e}^{(3)(2)-5} \\\\ & =- 12 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(-4{e}^{3x-5}-3){|}_{x=2} \\\\ & =-4{e}^{(3)(2)-5}-3 \\\\ & =- 4 e - 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(- 4 e - 3) & =(- 12 e)(x-(2)) \\\\ y-(- 4 e - 3) & =- 12 e x-(- 24 e) \\\\ y & =- 12 e x - 3 + 20 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
